issues.body:
Owner comment (2026-10-28), with a Play screenshot of 4 burnt/charred zombies standing in a tight row in the field, all in exactly the same pose at the same moment:

> no zombie will get an identical animation to anyone beside it like this. very ugly

**What the screenshot shows:** the group spawned together, so every zombie plays the same anim from the same start time at the same rate; they move like clones in lockstep (same arm, same step, same lean).

**Wanted:** neighbouring zombies never look identical:
- random start time / phase into the loop on spawn and after each state change (idle, walk, attack);
- small random play-rate per zombie (e.g. 0.85-1.15);
- pick from the variant anims of the QuokkaVoid pack (gaits, idles, attacks) per zombie instead of the same one;
- a bit of spawn spread so a group doesn't stand in a perfect line; optional slight scale/yaw jitter.
Applies to BP_Zombie (and the Colossus where it groups).

Done when: in Play, a freshly spawned group of 4+ zombies shows no two neighbours in the same pose at the same time, walking, idling or attacking.

